docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T03.log:2802:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:274:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BbdQyD8DbWiNRxRFHe822D","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now let me create a comprehensive summary. I have all the information needed.\n\n---\n\n## Lattice MCP Tools & Architecture Report\n\n### 1. **MCP Tools Surface** (38 tools total)\n\nGrouped by domain:\n\n**Workflow Planning & Discovery (8)**\n- `get_context_capsule` — first-touch unfamiliar code; returns pivots + handle\n- `prepare_change` — fix/add/refactor planning; edit files, tests, risks\n- `plan_edit` — patch-oriented planning; candidate spans, affected callers, stale docs\n- `get_working_set_context` — compress open files + symbols + tests into one bundle\n- `impact_from_diff` — analyze git diff impact + downstream dependents\n- `diagnose_failure` — triage stack traces, compiler errors, test failures to suspect symbols\n- `trace_scenario` — debug by behavior description; execution paths + guards + side effects\n- `summarize_subsystem` — unknown domain overview without full source reads\n\n**Memory & Observation (6)**\n- `save_observation` — persist session/branch/repo-scoped memory with structured fields\n- `list_observations` — retrieve all stored memories, newest first\n- `update_observation` — edit memory in-place, clear stale flags\n- `delete_observation` — remove obsolete memory\n- `refresh_memory` — update with fresh evidence while preserving ID\n- `promote_observation` — elevate session memory to branch/repo scope\n\n**Memory Retrieval (2)**\n- `get_session_context` — recall relevant memories for current + prior sessions\n- `search_memory` — keyword search across all sessions\n\n**Diagnostics & Metrics (2)**\n- `record_workflow_outcome` — save success/failure workflow outcomes for reuse\n- `get_session_metrics` — inspect tool-call counts, payload sizes, handle reuse rate\n\n**Graph Traversal (7)**\n- `get_symbol` — lookup symbol by name + file with full source\n- `get_skeleton` — token-efficient file structure: symbols, kinds, dependent counts\n- `get_dependencies` — outgoing dependency edges from a symbol\n- `get_dependents` — incoming dependents (who uses this symbol)\n- `get_impact_graph` — transitive dependents N-hops out\n- `search_symbols` — substring search across all symbol names\n- `search_logic_flow` — execution paths between function call chains\n\n**Documentation & Backlinks (5)**\n- `get_docs_capsule` — retrieve relevant engineering docs + mentioned symbols\n- `get_backlinks` — inbound references to symbol/file/doc/section\n- `get_outgoing_links` — outbound references from target\n- `find_stale_docs` — identify docs mentioning changed symbols/files\n- `find_relevant_tests` — tests anchored to files/symbols/diff\n\n**Context Handles & Expansion (1)**\n- `expand_context` — follow-up to workflow handle; narrow to specific symbol/file/test\n\n**Repo Rules & Metadata (3)**\n- `get_repo_playbook` — architecture, conventions, high-signal files, durable patterns\n- `get_project_rules` — repo-specific conventions and language setup\n- `workspace_setup` — workspace conventions, language breakdown, recommended config\n\n**Graph Management (2)**\n- `submit_lsp_edges` — enrich graph with LSP call-hierarchy edges (internal)\n- `index_status` — graph stats: node count, file count, language breakdown\n\n---\n\n### 2. **VS Code Extension Structure** (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/extension/src/`)\n\n**Files:**\n- `extension.ts` (861 lines) — activation, 12 command registrations, MCP tool dispatch\n- `daemon.ts` (395 lines) — JSON-RPC stdio manager, binary resolution, process lifecycle\n- `sidebar.ts` (810 lines) — sidebar webview: graph stats, memory clear, delivery mix metrics\n- `docsWorkbench.ts` (803 lines) — docs graph visualization, backlinks, outgoing links\n- `codelens.ts` — inline code lens for dependents\n- `hover.ts` — symbol hover provider with snippet context\n- `statusbar.ts` — VS Code status bar with node count\n\n**Command Registrations** (extension.ts lines 123–512):\n- `lattice.reindex` — trigger full workspace reindexing with polling\n- `lattice.showStatus` — display daemon status snapshot\n- `lattice.showDependents` — CodeLens action to list dependents\n- `lattice.prepareChange` — prompt for task, call `prepare_change`\n- `lattice.impactFromDiff` — analyze staged or working diff\n- `lattice.getWorkingSetContext` — compress visible editors\n- `lattice.diagnoseFailure` — paste error, get diagnostics\n- `lattice.expandContext` — expand prior context handle with new focus\n- `lattice.getDocsCapsule` — ask for docs\n- `lattice.showBacklinks`, `lattice.showOutgoingLinks` — docs navigation\n- `lattice.findStaleDocs` — check docs after changes\n- `lattice.openDocsWorkbench` — launch docs graph view\n\n---\n\n### 3. **JSON-RPC Stdio Communication** (daemon.ts)\n\n**Protocol:**\n- Request: `{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\", \"id\":N, \"method\":\"...\", \"params\":{...}}`\n- Response: `{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\", \"id\":N, \"result\":{...}}` or `{\"error\":{...}}`\n- **Newline-delimited** stdio; buffered by DaemonManager\n\n**Core Methods:**\n- `lattice/status` — daemon status snapshot (nodes, files, edges)\n- `lattice/reindex` — explicit workspace reindex\n- `lattice/dependents` — get dependents (daemon-side endpoint)\n- `tools/list` — get available MCP tool schemas\n- `tools/call` — dispatch tool with arguments; returns `McpToolResponse`\n\n**Tool Response Shape:**\n```typescript\ninterface McpToolResponse {\n    content?: Array<{ type?: string; text?: string }>;\n}\n```\nText content is parsed as JSON if valid, else returned as string.\n\n**Daemon Lifecycle:**\n- Binary resolved: extension/bin/lattice → PATH → daemon/target/debug/lattice\n- SHA-256 verification before spawn\n- Restart on crash (max 5 retries with backoff)\n- Process killed on extension deactivation\n\n---\n\n### 4. **UI Surfaces for Memory & Diagnostics**\n\n**Sidebar (sidebar.ts):**\n- Graph stats display: nodes, files, edges (live polling, 3s interval)\n- Delivery mix meter: \"X tiny · Y compact · Z full\" (tracks tool response size strategy)\n- Context handle reuse rate meter\n- Outcome memory reuse counter\n- \"Clear Memory\" button dispatches `lattice/clearMemory` request\n\n**Docs Workbench (docsWorkbench.ts):**\n- Renders backlinks & outgoing links graphs with preview snippets\n- Two-way navigation between docs targets\n- State: ready/loading/error/idle with focused node and link counts\n\n**Output Channel:**\n- Tool results displayed with title + separator\n- Context handle + origin logged when present\n- Results rendered as markdown (string) or JSON\n\n**CodeLens (codelens.ts):**\n- Inline \"Show dependents\" action on each symbol\n- Invokes `lattice.showDependents` command\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Compact vs Full Render Modes**\n\nBoth exposed in tool responses and controllable via `render` parameter:\n\n- `hybrid` (default) — markdown summary + JSON payload in response\n- `markdown` — summary text only\n- `json` — structured data only\n\nTools supporting this: `prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `get_context_capsule`, `diagnose_failure`, `impact_from_diff`, `trace_scenario`, `get_working_set_context`, `get_repo_playbook`, `summarize_subsystem`.\n\n**Size delivery strategy** (sidebar metric):\n- `tiny` — minimal context for quick recovery\n- `compact` — focused context for edit loops\n- `full` — exhaustive context for deep review\n\nTracked in `SessionMetrics` as `compact_task_count`, `widened_task_count`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Context Handle / expand_context Pattern**\n\n**Shape:**\n```json\n{\n  \"context_handle\": \"sha256-hex-...omitted...\",\n  \"context_origin\": \"prepare_change\" | \"get_context_capsule\" | \"impact_from_diff\" | ...\n}\n```\n\n**Where Emitted:**\n- All workflow bundles: `prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `get_context_capsule`, `diagnose_failure`, `impact_from_diff`, `trace_scenario`, `get_working_set_context`, `get_repo_playbook`, `summarize_subsystem`\n- Cached in `ContextHandleCache` (daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs)\n\n**expand_context Resolution (expansion.ts line 349–381):**\n- Extension stores `lastContextHandle` + `lastContextOrigin` after each tool call\n- User selects a focus target: `symbol:X`, `file:path/to/file.rs`, `memory:0`, `test:test_name`\n- `expand_context` with handle + focus narrows prior bundle to next delta\n- Supports `max_tokens` to control output size\n\n**Stable Handle Basis** (2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md):\n- Graph identity: `SymbolId { file, name, byte_offset }`\n- Deterministic encoding replaces name-only `symbol:<name>` fallback\n- Preferred by `expand_context` for exact resolution; legacy `file:` and `symbol:` forms remain backward compatible\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Architecture Docs** (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/architecture/`)\n\n| File | One-Line Summary |\n|------|------------------|\n| `2026-04-11-structured-memory.md` | Structured assertion layer: verification status, confidence reason, freshness policy, provenance, evidence; legacy memory remains compatible. |\n| `2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md` | Durable graph identity (file+name+byte_offset) replaces name-only targets; expand_context prefers exact stable handles. |\n| `2026-04-11-patch-oriented-planning.md` | plan_edit bundles candidate spans, affected callers, stale doc signals, tests for direct patching; compact/full modes. |\n| `2026-04-11-scenario-tracing.md` | trace_scenario debugs by behavior description; returns execution paths, guards, side effects, failure branches ranked by confidence. |\n| `2026-04-11-storage-and-search-backends.md` | SQLite durable source + USearch ANN vectors; FTS5 memory keyword search; vector scopes distinguish symbols from file summaries. |\n\n---\n\n**Summary:** Lattice exposes 38 MCP tools across 8 domains. Extension is 7 TypeScript files (~6KB total) with 12 command registrations, sidebar stats/metrics, docs graph workbench, and hover/CodeLens providers. JSON-RPC stdio transports tool calls; responses carry context handles for follow-up expansion. Memory is structured with verification, provenance, and freshness metadata. Render modes (compact/full/hybrid) and handle caching enable efficient reuse across edit loops."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"1ad64c16-15bf-4b60-b813-4dde65757801","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:19:12.013Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the Lattice VS Code extension at /home/pete/cadres/lattice/extension/ and the MCP tool surface in the daemon. Report:\n\n1. The full list of MCP tools currently exposed (search the daemon source for the tool registration). Group by domain: workflow, memory, docs, observation/event, diagnostics.\n2. The VS Code extension structure: src/ layout, main entry, command registrations, panels/views.\n3. How the extension communicates with the daemon (JSON-RPC stdio details).\n4. Any existing UI surfaces for memory inspection, observations, diagnostics, retrieval.\n5. The compact vs full render mode if it's surfaced in tool responses.\n6. The \"context handle\" / expand_context pattern — what shape, where used.\n7. Existing docs under /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/architecture/ that describe MCP contract, memory, retrieval, observations, or graph design — list them with one-line summaries.\n\nCite file paths. Be precise about the surface area. Report in under 700 words; this is groundwork for a build plan.","agentId":"a557448fbca2f582c","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now let me create a comprehensive summary. I have all the information needed.\n\n---\n\n## Lattice MCP Tools & Architecture Report\n\n### 1. **MCP Tools Surface** (38 tools total)\n\nGrouped by domain:\n\n**Workflow Planning & Discovery (8)**\n- `get_context_capsule` — first-touch unfamiliar code; returns piv