nds, budget catalog with fallback strategies, and the architecture doc at `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md`.\n- **T44**: scope-gated manual review queue for repo + organization.\n- **T45**: replay-safe execution, reversal, cached-provenance replay (live LLM never called).\n- **T46**: integration tests covering proposals, apply/reject, replay, queue bounds, failure events.\n- **R47**: review with required headings (`## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Proposal discipline`, `## LLM budget evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`).\n- **T48**: eight-state output model verbatim, file/symbol/doc/test existence, `verification_jobs` table.\n- **T49**: exact-span content hashing, encoding-flip distinguished from content change, no whole-file reads.\n- **T50**: `ScopeFilter` enforced at store boundary, negative tests for all four scopes, `MemoryScopeFiltered` event.\n- **T51**: time-bound expiry, incremental verification narrowed to changed files/symbols, bounded work budget, snapshot-id advance on success.\n- **T52**: `SurfacingPipeline::partition` enforcing trusted vs advisory split, exhaustive `classify` match, ranker hard precondition excluding non-`Verified`.\n- **T53**: integration tests proving stale never trusted + scope leakage blocked across all eight states and all four scopes.\n- **R54**: review with required headings (`## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Stale-label discipline`, `## Scope-leak evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`).\n- **R55**: cross-layer contract gate with required headings; ships new test file `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` per tasks.json `files_expected`.\n\nNo code was implemented; tasks.json, context.md, and plan.md were not modified."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a163eb6f432e922f5 (use SendMessage with to: 'a163eb6f432e922f5' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 121791\ntool_uses: 37\nduration_ms: 848530</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"569d5d02-ce86-46eb-9622-7ea8cc55e105","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:46:35.675Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are writing markdown task brief files for a build harness. Do NOT implement the feature itself — just write the brief markdown files.\n\nRepo root: /home/pete/cadres/lattice\nSpec: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md  (READ Phases 6 and 7 sections + §Consolidation Engine + §Verification Engine especially \"LLM-driven consolidation\" subsection)\nContext: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/context.md\nTasks JSON: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks.json\nShared standards: /home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md\n\nWrite these 16 files at `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/<TASK_ID>.md`:\n\nT39, T40, T41, T42, T43, T44, T45, T46, R47, T48, T49, T50, T51, T52, T53, R54, R55\n\nThat's 17 files — write all of them.\n\n**Use the same template structure as prior agents** (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks, Definition of done).\n\n**Task-specific guidance:**\n\n- T39 — consolidation job runtime: proposal model means NO silent writes; every LLM-driven job produces a proposal record requiring explicit apply or reject. Tables: `consolidation_jobs`. Queue is bounded (drops new jobs when full per spec, with log warning).\n- T40 — synchronous session consolidation: episode summaries on small task traces only. NOT on hot path (per spec §Phase 2 DoD ≤5ms budget).\n- T41 — deterministic jobs: duplicate detection, supersession candidates, demote unused/low-value memories, mark stale memories after graph changes, refresh memories whose evidence still matches.\n- T42 — LLM-driven jobs: episode summary, procedure extraction from repeated successful workflows, contradiction detection, failure-pattern extraction. MUST run only in background or manual-review modes, never on synchronous post-task hot path.\n- T43 — LLM provenance: each proposal records model, prompt hash, response hash. Queue depth bounded. Cost and latency budgets documented per job type in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md`. Failed/malformed responses leave prior memory unchanged and emit consolidation failure event.\n- T44 — manual review queue for high-scope (repo + organization) memory changes.\n- T45 — replay-safe execution: jobs can be replayed; provenance + prior state preserved.\n- T46 — integration tests: proposals, apply/reject, replay, queue bounds, failure events.\n- R47 — Phase 6 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Proposal discipline`, `## LLM budget evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- T48 — verification engine core: file/symbol/doc/test existence checks. Outputs from spec §Verification Engine: verified/unverified/in_review/stale/contradicted/superseded/expired/invalidated.\n- T49 — exact-span evidence validation: when evidence captured an exact span, validate the span text still matches.\n- T50 — branch/workspace scope enforcement (deny leakage). Negative tests required.\n- T51 — time-bound expiry + incremental verification triggered by graph changes (large repos cannot tolerate full rescans).\n- T52 — stale surfacing in workflow bundles + label discipline: stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as trusted guidance. Non-negotiable from spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties.\n- T53 — integration tests: stale never displayed as trusted; scope leakage blocked.\n- R54 — Phase 7 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Stale-label discipline`, `## Scope-leak evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- R55 — contract gate Memory ↔ Verification ↔ Retrieval. Required headings: `## Contract surfaces`, `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Stale-label round-trip`, `## Scope-filter round-trip`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`. Adds new test file `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` per tasks.json `files_expected`.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact text. Quote it.\n\nFor each task: 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths from tasks.json, exact verification commands from tasks.json. Coding-standard checks must include the standard limits (file ≤800, function ≤50, nesting ≤3) and no-broken-windows rules.\n\nWrite all 17 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code.","agentId":"a163eb6f432e922f5","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 17 task brief files written successfully.\n\n**Files written: 17**\n\nFirst 3 paths confirmed:\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T39.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T40.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md`\n\nAll 17 files exist (T39, T40, T41, T42, T43, T44, T45, T46, R47, T48, T49, T50, T51, T52, T53, R54, R55) under `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/`.\n\nEach brief follows the prior-agent template (Goal, Spec excerpts that drive this task, Inputs, Steps with 5-10 concrete steps, Files expected, Verification with exact commands from tasks.json, Coding-standard checks citing the ≤800-line/≤50-line/≤3-nesting/≤10-cyclomatic limits and no-broken-windows rules, Definition of done checklist).\n\nKey task-specific points encoded as required:\n- **T39**: proposal-only model, `consolidation_jobs` + `consolidation_proposals` tables, bounded queue drops with warn log.\n- **T40**: synchronous deterministic episode template only, ≤5ms hot-path budget, LLM-forbid guard.\n- **T41**: deterministic scanners (duplicates, supersession, demotion, stale-marker, refresh) all routing through T39 proposals; `stale_marker.rs` + `refresh.rs` ship in this task per spec bullets.\n- **T42**: four LLM jobs with mode guard forbidding synchronous mode; malformed responses leave memory unchanged and emit `ConsolidationFailed` event.\n- **T43**: SHA-256 prompt/response hashes, per-kind queue bounds, budget catalog with fallback strategies, and the architecture doc at `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md`.\n- **T44**: scope-gated manual review queue for repo + organization.\n- **T45**: replay-safe execution, reversal, cached-provenance replay (live LLM never called).\n- **T46**: integration tests covering proposals, apply/reject, replay, queue bounds, failure events.\n- **R47**: review with required headings (`## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Proposal discipline`, `## LLM budget evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`).\n- **T48**: eight-state output model verbatim, file/symbol/doc/test existence, `verification_jobs` table.\n- **T49**: exact-span content hashing, encoding-flip distinguished from content change, no whole-file reads.\n- **T50**: `ScopeFilter` enforced at store boundary, negative tests for all four scopes, `MemoryScopeFiltered` event.\n- **T51**: time-bound expiry, incremental verification narrowed to changed files/symbols, bounded work budget, snapshot-id advance on success.\n- **T52**: `SurfacingPipeline::partition` enforcing trusted vs advisory split, exhaustive `classify` match, ranker hard precondition excluding non-`Verified`.\n- **T53**: integration tests proving stale never trusted + scope leakage blocked across all eight states and all four scopes.\n- **R54**: review with required headings (`## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Stale-label discipline`, `## Scope-leak evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`).\n- **R55**: cross-layer contract gate with required headings; ships new test file `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` per tasks.json `files_expected`.\n\nNo code was implemented; tasks.json, context.md, and plan.md were not modified."}],"totalDurationMs":848530,"totalTokens":121791,"totalToolUseCount":37,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1191,"cache_read_input_tokens":119194,"output_tokens":1405,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1191},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1405,"cache_read_input_tokens":119194,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1191,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":13,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":4,"editFileCount":17,"linesAdded":1295,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
