 doc + final MCP reference. Required headings: `## Final tool list`, `## Audit findings`, `## Collapsed tools`. Documents which tools were collapsed and why per spec §Phase 8 \"Tool surface discipline\".\n- T62 — workflow outcome recording integrated by default + composition tests.\n- R63 — Phase 8 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Tool-surface size`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- R64 — contract gate MCP schema regression. Required headings: `## Schema surfaces`, `## Render-mode coverage` (compact/full/diagnostic/handles for every tool), `## Backward-compatibility shims`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`. New test file `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_schema_tests.rs`.\n- T65 — metric collection: all required signals from spec §Phase 9 \"Required metrics\": tool calls per successful task, irrelevant files opened per task, relevant anchor recall, memory inclusion precision, memory later-used rate, stale memory surfaced rate, contradiction missed rate, tests recommended vs needed, workflow success after first plan.\n- T66 — benchmark task fixture repository: cross-language (Rust, TypeScript, Python). Golden anchors JSON per spec §Risks \"Overfitting To Current Repo\" control.\n- T67 — `get_memory_metrics` + retrieval relevance surfaces wired through MCP.\n- T68 — regression dashboard CLI (`lattice_report` binary) + architecture doc.\n- T69 — metrics regression coverage tests asserting spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets: 30% fewer discovery calls, 40% fewer irrelevant reads, 80% memory precision, zero trusted display of stale/contradicted, 90% correct relevant-test recommendation.\n- R70 — Phase 9 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Success-criteria coverage`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact text. Quote it.\n\nFor each task: 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths from tasks.json, exact verification commands from tasks.js