ment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Tool-surface size`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict` headings.\n- R64 includes required `## Schema surfaces`, `## Render-mode coverage` (compact/full/diagnostic/handles matrix), `## Backward-compatibility shims`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict` headings and produces the new `mcp_schema_tests.rs`.\n- T65 lists all nine spec §Phase 9 \"Required metrics\" signals as deterministic collectors with `MetricValue.value: Option<f64>` for honest null reporting.\n- T66 covers spec §Risks \"Overfitting To Current Repo\" with three language fixtures (rust/typescript/python) plus `golden_anchors.json` schema and freeze policy.\n- T67 wires T65 through MCP and adds per-call ranking-signal breakdowns per spec §Retrieval Engine.\n- T68 implements `lattice_report` CLI binary with text/json/ci-summary formats, `--fail-on-regression`, encoded spec §Measurable Success Criteria thresholds.\n- T69 ships one `#[test]` per spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target (30% / 40% / 80% / 0 / 0 / 90%) sourcing thresholds from T68's `SuccessCriteriaThresholds` rather than hard-coding twice.\n- R70 includes required `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Success-criteria coverage`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict` headings and a per-target threshold matrix.\n\nEvery brief includes the standard Cadres coding-standard checks (file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10, schema parity, no broken windows, no `TODO`/`FIXME`, observability spans). All verification commands match tasks.json exactly. tasks.json, context.md, and plan.md were not modified."}],"totalDurationMs":805668,"totalTokens":119701,"totalToolUseCount":32,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":730,"cache_read_input_tokens":117591,"output_tokens":1379,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":730},"inference_geo":"","iterat